Author: Olof Johansson <olof@lixom.net>
Date:   Thu Sep 24 19:51:27 2026 -0700

    F13: the NavigationStack re-applied the bottom safe area; the page takes 10pt of it back

    The root's .ignoresSafeArea(.container, edges: .bottom) sat outside the
    NavigationStack, which hands its content the window's 34pt bottom inset
    again. The page now ignores it inside the stack and pads back all but
    10pt, ending 24pt above the edge, clear of the home indicator. L1's
    inset-probe test asserts the 24pt gap. L1: passed in 270s.

diff --git a/app/App/Browser/DashboardRootView.swift b/app/App/Browser/DashboardRootView.swift
